# Dev-tooling secrets for THIS repo — copy to `.env` beside this file and fill in.
#
#   cp .proactive-jupi/.env.template .proactive-jupi/.env
#
# Lives here because everything Proactive-Jupi owns lives under .proactive-jupi/.
# `.env` is gitignored; `.env.template` (this file) is committed and must never
# hold a real value. Nothing the plugin ships at runtime reads this file: the
# skills reach Supermemory through the installed MCP connector. It exists only
# for repo scripts you run by hand — the eval teardown in evals/*/purge-scratch.sh
# and any direct HTTP-API maintenance (bulk delete, correcting a Fact).
#
# Deliberately NOT in .proactive-jupi/config.local.json: that file gets mirrored
# into unattended/cloud run CWDs, so an admin-scoped key would travel with every
# scheduled routine. Keep it here instead.

# Supermemory admin key — https://app.supermemory.ai → API keys. Format: sm_...
# Used by: evals/update-brain/purge-scratch.sh (purge a container tag),
#          ad-hoc HTTP-API ops (https://api.supermemory.ai/v3/...).
SUPERMEMORY_API_KEY=

# Jupi workspace slug that eval runs post and finalize fixture decisions into —
# NEVER the real workspace in config.local.json (`jupiWorkspace`). Unlike Neon rows
# and Supermemory containers, a Jupi decision can't be bulk-deleted, and decisions
# are what teammates read — so isolation here has to be the workspace itself, set
# before the run. See evals/README.md.
# Used by: every behavioral eval that touches Jupi (act-or-decide, act-post-decision,
#          setup-proactive-jupi).
JUPI_EVAL_WORKSPACE=
